:" succeeds, only its final state commits","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"if both legs fail, both shadows are discarded, the starting ","type":"text"},{"code":"RouteStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remains unchanged, and the fallback failure is returned","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" routes each attempted leg recursively through middleware; direct ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationEngine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" execution has no middleware","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"single-command execution only emits the successful leg’s committed state change","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"transaction execution keeps public middleware observation commit-only, while discarded preview legs run internal cleanup","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For direct and batch store execution, the folded ","type":"text"},{"code":"didExecute","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" result decides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether a leg succeeded. Transaction execution must choose and commit from its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preview result so ","type":"text"},{"code":"didExecute","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays commit-only; a post-commit fold changes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported result but cannot reopen fallback selection or undo the commit.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"executedCommands","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an attempt log, not a commit log. It records effective","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"commands passed to the engine, including attempts later discarded by either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"savepoint or transaction rollback; middleware interceptions cancelled before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the engine are not included. The savepoint protects ","type":"text"},{"code":"RouteStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" authority, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arbitrary side effects performed by attempt-level middleware callbacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".whenCancelled"},{"text":" when rollback-to-fallback semantics belong to one logical command.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Batch-semantics","level":2,"text":"Batch semantics","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationBatchExecutor.executeBatch(_:stopOnFailure:)"},{"text":" is for observation batching.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Batch execution still runs commands one step at a time, but it lets higher layers coalesce observation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"step middleware still runs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"stopOnFailure: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps later commands running after a failure"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"stopOnFailure: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stops the batch after the first failed step"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the store emits aggregated "},{"code":".changed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":".batchExecuted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cases"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through "},{"code":"onEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the caller gets a structured "},{"code":"NavigationBatchResult","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use batch execution when the caller wants one “transition event” while still preserving per-step execution.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Transaction-semantics","level":2,"text":"Transaction semantics","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationTransactionExecutor.executeTransaction(_:)"},{"text":" is the atomic option.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Transactions:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reject an empty command list as uncommitted, with no failure index because no step ran"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"preview commands on a shadow stack"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"abort on the first failure or cancellation"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"leave the real state unchanged on failure"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"commit the final state all at once on success"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"surface public "},{"code":"didExecute","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ transaction observation only for committed leaves"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"run internal discard cleanup for previewed leaves that never commit"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use transactions when all-or-nothing semantics are required.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Typed-failures","level":2,"text":"Typed failures","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core legality failures stay in typed results instead of exceptions:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationResult.emptyStack","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationResult.invalidPopCount(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationResult.insufficientStackDepth(requested:available:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationResult.routeNotFound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationResult.cancelled(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This keeps navigation failure in normal control flow and makes policy handling easy to pattern-match.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/Command-Batch-and-Transaction-Semantics"},"abstract":[{"text":"InnoRouter exposes three different execution semantics on purpose.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting"],["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting","doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/InnoRouterCore"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/innoroutercore\/command-batch-and-transaction-semantics"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core/documentation/InnoRouterCore/InnoRouterCore":{"title":"InnoRouterCore","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/InnoRouterCore","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/innoroutercore\/innoroutercore","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"State, command, result, and execution primitives for InnoRouter."}]},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core/documentat